ls - list what is in a directory

SYNOPSIS
    ls [-l] [DIRECTORY]

DESCRIPTION
    Lists the current directory, or the one named.

      -l   one entry per line, with its mode, owner, size and date

    Without -l, a directory is shown with a trailing / and a symbolic link
    with a trailing @, so the three kinds are told apart without a second
    column.

    A long listing describes the link itself rather than what it points at,
    and shows the target after an arrow. That is deliberate: a link that
    leads nowhere would otherwise be indistinguishable from a missing file.

SEE ALSO
    cat, stat, find, ln
